      "answer": "Based on the provided excerpts, **no evaluation results are reported in this paper**. The measurement campaign is still in progress.\n\nKey evidence:\n- Excerpt [3] explicitly states: \"Results are not reported here: the measurement campaign is still running, and the sections that will carry it are deferred to the full version of the paper.\" [3]\n- Excerpt [4] confirms: \"The campaign is in progress; no latency, utilisation or energy results are claimed, and the expected relationships are stated as hypotheses.\" [4]\n\nThe paper does describe the **planned evaluation metrics** [5] and **statistical analysis approach** [1, 2]:\n- **Latency metrics**: mean, P95, P99, and jitter (standard deviation of per-request latency) [5]\n- **Background cost**: completion time relative to isolated baseline [5]\n- **Mechanism metrics**: utilisation and context-switch counts [5]\n- **Energy proxy**: RAPL register readings where available [5]\n- **Statistical approach**: rank-based procedures (pairwise rank test, multi-sample analogue), bootstrap resampling for confidence intervals on percentiles, effect size reporting alongside significance [1, 2]\n- **Success criterion**: a configuration counts as useful if it moves P95 across the SLO [2]\n\nHowever, no actual numerical results, comparisons, or findings are presented in these excerpts.",
